{"author":{"id":"f943aa1c5ee078b881a8e97535a4e2ccb401d01ca00f4128126befa9cca58a32"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792670746,"nonce":"0Bk9eAuIpEWzLkhPBw5lLokT7/M=","message":"## Handover: M4, tests and checks (branch b768fbb-m4-tests-and-checks)\n\nStep 4 now runs the tests and checks that the base branch's `.git-board.toml` declares (`[cycle.tests.\u003csuite\u003e]`, `[cycle.checks.\u003cname\u003e]`). Each run happens in a clean `git worktree add --detach` of the branch's last commit. Its result is a signed line in `refs/notes/ci/\u003cwriter\u003e` (ADR 0001). Mark ready for review is a server POST that refuses until every check is proven at the head. `git board verify` prints the same verdict from the command line. M1's test-file globs were renamed `[cycle] test-files`.\n\n### Checked\n\n- In a browser, on a clone of git-board-test in $TMPDIR (origin removed, so no live calls), at 1440 and 900px:\n  - a bug issue: the touched suite and check came pre-ticked;\n  - \"Run at \u003ctest commit\u003e\" gave FAIL, then the head gave PASS;\n  - Mark ready for review was refused, first with \"lint not run at …\", then with \"lint FAILED, signed by alice\";\n  - after the fix, lint passed and the issue moved to in-review;\n  - a feature issue showed the per-criterion rule and reused lint's PASS through the content key.\n- `git board verify` agrees with the page: proven at the head; exit 1 with the FAILED reason at the fix-with-TODO commit.\n- `make ci`: green except TestIssueSyncTakesTheAssigneesMode and TestForgeSyncSetsTheAssigneesMode, which fail on origin/main too. Its first run also caught TestAppendParallel leaking `ci-tmp` refs under load; the private ref now has no reflog and a longer packed-refs wait (bfbf51a), checked with 72 stressed runs. Web: typecheck is clean, 166/166 tests pass.\n\n### Changed beyond the plan\n\n- Files are matched by git glob pathspecs (`:(glob)`), not a new matcher.\n- The key carries a `dir` line.\n- The run POST takes `target: head|test`.\n- A `.pub` signingkey is accepted when its private key sits beside it.\n- The compare-and-swap retries until a deadline, not 10 times.\n- Tools are not in the key; they stay in the line.\n- The gate skips `where = \"ci\"` checks.\n- Propose skips sh/bash scripts. Its Makefile and package.json set is lint/vet/typecheck/type-check, and lefthook's `glob:` is not mapped.\n- verify computes the base with the git CLI, so a held git-bug lock doesn't stop it.\n- The browser check turned up four fixes, all in f3a84b6:\n  - step 4's wait is now worded by the kind's rule: \"write the tests\" for a feature, \"write the failing test\" for a bug;\n  - a card refusal no longer follows you to another step;\n  - the gate's time is local;\n  - an empty log reads \"(no output)\".\n\n### Left for later branches\n\n- Pushing and fetching `refs/notes/ci/*` with sync. The reader already takes the union of `refs/notes/remotes/*/ci/*`. The push command in docs/configuration.md was not run live, because pushes are denied in this sandbox.\n- The live-worktree feedback run; only the recorded run is built.\n- ssh-agent keys and literal `key::` signing keys are refused with a message.\n- `refs/notes/ci-tmp/*` refs left by a crash are not pruned.\n- A PATCH of the status (or a drag on the board) bypasses the gate; only the step's button is gated.\n- The land's sample re-run and the agents' deny rules belong to wtx. The run at the merged head is M6.\n- Once 0aa3715 lands: rebase, then Propose on git-board's own lefthook.yml.\n\n### Seen, not M4\n\n- TestIssueSyncTakesTheAssigneesMode and TestForgeSyncSetsTheAssigneesMode fail on origin/main too.\n- At 900px the header's Inbox overlaps Sync, and the \"Updated just now\" toast covers the bottom-left Run button.\n","files":null}]}